\section*{Grain boundary diffusion}

To investigate grain boundary (GB) diffusion, we first computed the GB energies of two low \(\Sigma\) twist GB configurations- \(\Sigma 4\) [1000] and \(\Sigma 7\) [0001]. Both configurations are fully relaxed using DFT and eSNAP. The eSNAP-calculated GB energies for twist \(\Sigma 4\) [1000] and \(\Sigma 7\) [0001] GBs are 1.41 and \(0.85 \mathrm{~J} \mathrm{~m}^{-2}\), respectively, in good agreement with the DFT values of 1.64 and \(0.86 \mathrm{Jm}^{-2}\), respectively.

